@@ -0,0 +1,524 @@
+# Multicore Fastboot User Guide
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [Overview](#overview)
+- [Quick Start](#quick-start)
+- [Configuration Methods](#configuration-methods)
+- [Usage Examples](#usage-examples)
+- [Configuration Reference](#configuration-reference)
+- [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting)
+- [Advanced Usage](#advanced-usage)
+
+## Overview
+
+The Multicore Fastboot feature allows you to boot multiple images on different Cortex-A cores simultaneously on i.MX platforms. This is useful for:
+
+- Running RTOS on secondary cores alongside U-Boot/Linux on the primary core
+- Running multiple RTOS instances on different cores
+- Bare-metal applications on specific cores
+- Asymmetric Multi-Processing (AMP) configurations
+
+### What You Can Do
+
+- Boot up to one images on each Cortex-A Cores
+- Choose whether Core 0 runs U-Boot or a custom image
+- Mix and match: U-Boot + RTOS, multiple RTOS, or any combination
+- Configure via simple configuration files or command line parameters
+
+## Quick Start
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+1. **Configure U-Boot with fastboot support** (if running U-Boot on Core 0):
+   ```kconfig
+   CONFIG_EMBEDDED_FASTBOOT_BLOB=y
+   CONFIG_EMBEDDED_FASTBOOT_BLOB_SIZE=256
+   ```
+
+2. **Your binary images** ready (e.g., RTOS binaries, bare-metal apps)
+
+3. **Know your memory addresses** where each image should be loaded
+
+4. Copy the other ensential images to imx-mkimage/iMX93 folder, for example u-boot.bin, u-boot-spl.bin, bl31.bin, DDR firmware, etc.
+
+### Basic Example: U-Boot + One RTOS
+
+**Scenario**: Run U-Boot on Core 0, FreeRTOS on Core 1
+
+```bash
+# Method 1: Using configuration file
+cd imx-mkimage
+copy the image to be run on Core 1 to imx-mkimage/iMX93 folder and rename it to be ca55_rtos0_img.bin
+make clean
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot fastboot=fastboot_uboot_1_rtos.mak
+
+# Method 2: Using command line parameters
+cd imx-mkimage
+make clean
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG=ca55_rtos0_img.bin \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000
+```
+
+That's it! The build system will:
+1. Create fastboot entries for your cores
+2. Embed boot entryies into U-Boot
+3. Add all images to the boot container
+4. Generate `flash.bin` ready to flash
+
+### Basic Example: Multiple RTOS and no U-Boot
+
+**Scenario**: Run RTOS on Core 0, another RTOS on Core 1
+
+```bash
+# Method 1: Using configuration file
+cd imx-mkimage
+copy the image to be run on Core 1 to imx-mkimage/iMX93 folder and rename it to be ca55_rtos0_img.bin, and copy the image to be run on Core 0 to imx-mkimage/iMX93 folder and rename it to be ca55_rtos1_img.bin
+make clean
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot fastboot=fastboot_2_rtos.mak
+
+# Method 2: Using command line parameters
+cd imx-mkimage
+make clean
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     CA_CORE0_IMG=ca55_rtos1_img.bin \
+     CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD1000000 \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG=ca55_rtos0_img.bin \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000
+```
+
+That's it! The build system will:
+1. Create fastboot entries for your cores
+2. Embed boot entries into dummy U-Boot as no U-Boot on Core 0
+3. Add all images to the boot container
+4. Generate `flash.bin` ready to flash
+
+### Flash to Device
+
+For i.MX93 boards, flash the generated `flash.bin`:
+```bash
+# For SD card (replace /dev/sdX with your SD card device)
+sudo dd if=flash.bin of=/dev/sdX bs=1k seek=32 conv=fsync
+
+# For eMMC (from U-Boot prompt)
+=> tftp ${loadaddr} flash.bin
+=> setexpr blkcnt ${filesize} + 0x1ff && setexpr blkcnt ${blkcnt} / 0x200
+=> mmc dev 0
+=> mmc write ${loadaddr} 0x40 ${blkcnt}
+```
+
+## Configuration Methods
+
+You have two ways to configure fastboot:
+
+### Method 1: Configuration File (Recommended for Reuse)
+
+For iMX93, it provides two default configuration file: `fastboot_uboot_1_rtos.mak` and `fastboot_2_rtos.mak`.
+Could use these default configuration files directly, or copy them and customize as needed:
+
+```makefile:iMX93/my_fastboot_config.mak
+# Core 0: FreeRTOS
+CA_CORE0_IMG = freertos.bin
+CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR = 0xD0000000
+
+# Core 1: Zephyr
+CA_CORE1_IMG = zephyr.bin
+CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR = 0xD1000000
+
+# Not Embed in U-Boot as Core0 not run U-Boot
+FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT = no
+```
+
+Build with:
+```bash
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot fastboot=my_fastboot_config.mak
+```
+
+### Method 2: Command Line Parameters (Quick Testing)
+
+Specify parameters directly on the command line:
+
+```bash
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     CA_CORE0_IMG=freertos.bin \
+     CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000 \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG=zephyr.bin \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD1000000 \
+     FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT=no
+```
+
+### Method 3: Hybrid (Override Config File)
+
+Use a config file but override specific values:
+
+```bash
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     fastboot=my_fastboot_config.mak \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD2000000  # Override address
+```
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Example 1: U-Boot + Single RTOS
+
+**Scenario**: U-Boot on Core 0, FreeRTOS on Core 1
+
+```bash
+# Prepare your binary
+cp /path/to/freertos.bin iMX93/
+
+# Build
+make clean
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG=freertos.bin \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000
+```
+
+**What happens**:
+- Core 0: Boots U-Boot (default)
+- Core 1: Boots FreeRTOS at 0xD0000000
+- Fastboot entries embedded in U-Boot
+- `FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT` automatically set to `yes`
+
+### Example 2: Two Independent RTOS (No U-Boot)
+
+**Scenario**: RTOS on Core 0, another RTOS on Core 1
+
+```bash
+cd iMX93
+make clean
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     CA_CORE0_IMG=rtos_core0.bin \
+     CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000 \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG=rtos_core1.bin \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD1000000
+```
+
+**What happens**:
+- Core 0: Boots rtos_core0.bin at 0xD0000000
+- Core 1: Boots rtos_core1.bin at 0xD1000000
+- No U-Boot involved
+- `FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT` automatically set to `no`
+- Dummy file created to carry fastboot entries
+
+### Example 3: U-Boot + Multiple RTOS
+
+**Scenario**: U-Boot on Core 0, RTOS on Cores 1, 2, and 3
+
+Create config file:
+```makefile:iMX9xx/fastboot_multi_rtos.mak
+# Core 1: Real-time processing
+CA_CORE1_IMG = rt_processing.bin
+CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR = 0xD0000000
+
+# Core 2: Data acquisition
+CA_CORE2_IMG = data_acq.bin
+CA_CORE2_IMG_LOAD_ADDR = 0xD1000000
+
+# Core 3: Communication
+CA_CORE3_IMG = comm.bin
+CA_CORE3_IMG_LOAD_ADDR = 0xD2000000
+
+# Embed in U-Boot
+FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT = yes
+```
+
+Build:
+```bash
+make clean
+make SOC=iMX9xx flash_singleboot fastboot=fastboot_multi_rtos.mak
+```
+
+## Configuration Reference
+
+### Required Parameters
+
+For each core you want to configure:
+
+| Parameter | Description | Example |
+|-----------|-------------|---------|
+| `CA_CORE<N>_IMG` | Path to binary image for Core N | `freertos.bin` |
+| `CA_CORE<N>_IMG_LOAD_ADDR` | Load address for Core N (hex) | `0xD0000000` |
+
+**Important**: If you set `CA_CORE<N>_IMG`, you **must** also set `CA_CORE<N>_IMG_LOAD_ADDR`, otherwise the build will fail.
+
+### Optional Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Description | Default | Values |
+|-----------|-------------|---------|--------|
+| `FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT` | Where to store fastboot entries | Auto | `yes` or `no` |
+
+**Default behavior**:
+- If `CA_CORE0_IMG` is **not set**: defaults to `yes` (Core 0 runs U-Boot, embed entries in U-Boot)
+- If `CA_CORE0_IMG` **is set**: defaults to `no` (Core 0 runs custom image, create dummy file)
+
+### Supported Cores
+
+You can configure any combination of cores from 0 to 15:
+- `CA_CORE0_IMG` / `CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR`
+- `CA_CORE1_IMG` / `CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR`
+- `CA_CORE2_IMG` / `CA_CORE2_IMG_LOAD_ADDR`
+- ...
+- `CA_CORE15_IMG` / `CA_CORE15_IMG_LOAD_ADDR`
+
+## Boot Sequence
+
+Understanding the boot sequence is important for system initialization and inter-core communication.
+
+The multicore fastboot follows a specific boot order to boot each core listed in the fastboot entries:
+1. **Secondary cores (Core 1, 2, 3, ...) boot first**
+- Boot in ascending order for each secondary core listed in fastboot entries: Core 1 → Core 2 → Core 3 → ...
+
+2. **Primary core (Core 0) boots last**
+- **Always boots last**, regardless of configuration
+- If `CA_CORE0_IMG` is not set: boots U-Boot
+- If `CA_CORE0_IMG` is set: boots the specified custom image
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Error: Missing Load Address
+
+```
+ERROR: CA_CORE1_IMG is set to 'freertos.bin' but CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR is not set
+```
+
+**Solution**: Always specify both image and load address:
+```bash
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG=freertos.bin \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000  # Add this
+```
+
+### Error: Invalid Configuration
+
+```
+ERROR: FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT is set to 'no' but CA_CORE0_IMG is not set.
+```
+
+**Explanation**: If Core 0 runs U-Boot (no `CA_CORE0_IMG`), fastboot entries must be embedded in U-Boot.
+
+**Solution**: Either:
+1. Remove `FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT=no` (let it auto-default to `yes`)
+2. Or specify a Core 0 image:
+   ```bash
+   CA_CORE0_IMG=core0.bin \
+   CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000 \
+   FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT=no
+   ```
+
+### Warning: Conflicting Configuration
+
+```
+WARNING: Conflicting fastboot configuration!
+CA_CORE0_IMG is set to: core0.bin
+FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT is set to: yes
+```
+
+**Explanation**: You specified a custom image for Core 0, but asked to embed entries in U-Boot. This is unusual.
+
+**Solution**: Change to `FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT=no`:
+```bash
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     CA_CORE0_IMG=core0.bin \
+     CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000 \
+     FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT=no  # Change this
+```
+
+### Error: U-Boot Missing Reservation
+
+```
+Error: Invalid magic number at offset 0x10 in u-boot.bin
+       Target file does not have a valid fastboot entries reservation
+```
+
+**Cause**: Your U-Boot was not built with fastboot support.
+
+**Solution**: Rebuild U-Boot with:
+```kconfig
+CONFIG_EMBEDDED_FASTBOOT_BLOB=y
+CONFIG_EMBEDDED_FASTBOOT_BLOB_SIZE=256
+```
+
+**Verify**:
+```bash
+xxd -s 0x10 -l 4 u-boot.bin
+# Should show: 46 53 42 54 (magic number)
+```
+
+### Boot Fails After Flashing
+
+**Debug steps**:
+
+1. **Verify flash.bin**:
+   ```bash
+   ./mkimage_imx8 -soc IMX9 -parse iMX93/flash.bin
+   ```
+
+2. **Check fastboot entries**:
+   ```bash
+   ../multicore_fastboot_tool --dump u-boot-fastboot.bin --offset 0x10
+   ```
+
+3. **Verify addresses are in valid RAM**:
+   - Check your platform's memory map
+   - Ensure no overlap between images
+
+4. **Test without fastboot**:
+   ```bash
+   make clean
+   make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot  # Without fastboot
+   # If this works, issue is in fastboot configuration
+   ```
+
+5. **Check serial console output** for boot errors
+
+## Advanced Usage
+
+### Inspecting Fastboot Entries
+
+View entries in a built image:
+
+```bash
+cd imx-mkimage
+./multicore_fastboot_tool --dump iMX93/u-boot-fastboot.bin --offset 0x10
+```
+
+Output:
+```
+========================================
+Fastboot Entry File Dump
+========================================
+File: u-boot-fastboot.bin
+File size: 524288 bytes
+========================================
+
+Header Information:
+----------------------------------------
+Magic:           0x54425346 ('FSBT') [VALID]
+Version:         0x0001 [VALID]
+Entry count:     2
+Checksum:        0x12345678 [VALID]
+
+Boot Entries:
+----------------------------------------
+Core ID  Entry Address      Flags      Reserved
+-------  -----------------  ---------- ----------
+1        0x00000000D0000000 0x00000000 0x00000000
+2        0x00000000D1000000 0x00000000 0x00000000
+========================================
+```
+
+### Extracting Images from Container
+
+```bash
+cd iMX93
+./mkimage_imx8 -soc IMX9 -extract flash.bin
+cd extracted_imgs
+ls -lh
+```
+
+### Using Pre-built Configuration Files
+
+The repository includes ready-to-use configurations:
+
+```bash
+# U-Boot + 1 RTOS
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot fastboot=fastboot_uboot_1_rtos.mak
+
+# 2 RTOS (no U-Boot)
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot fastboot=fastboot_2_rtos.mak
+```
+
+Customize them by copying:
+```bash
+cd iMX93
+cp fastboot_uboot_1_rtos.mak my_config.mak
+# Edit my_config.mak
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot fastboot=my_config.mak
+```
+
+### Verifying Your Configuration
+
+Before building, verify your setup:
+
+```bash
+# Check that all required files exist
+ls -lh iMX93/freertos.bin
+ls -lh iMX93/u-boot.bin
+
+# Verify U-Boot has fastboot support (if using embedded mode)
+xxd -s 0x10 -l 4 iMX93/u-boot.bin
+
+# Do a dry run to see what will be built
+make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG=freertos.bin \
+     CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000 \
+     --dry-run
+```
+
+## Summary
+
+**Quick Reference**:
+
+| Scenario | Command |
+|----------|---------|
+| U-Boot + 1 RTOS | `make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot CA_CORE1_IMG=rtos.bin CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000` |
+| 2 RTOS (no U-Boot) | `make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot CA_CORE0_IMG=rtos0.bin CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD0000000 CA_CORE1_IMG=rtos1.bin CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR=0xD1000000` |
+| Use config file | `make SOC=iMX93 flash_singleboot fastboot=my_config.mak` |
+| Inspect entries | `./multicore_fastboot_tool --dump u-boot-fastboot.bin --offset 0x10` |
+
+**Remember**:
+- Always specify both `IMG` and `IMG_LOAD_ADDR` for each core
+- Let `FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT` auto-default unless you have a specific reason
+- Verify your U-Boot has fastboot support if using embedded mode
+- Check memory addresses don't overlap
+- Use serial console to debug boot issues
+
+For more details on the binary format and internal implementation, see the [Technical Appendix](#technical-appendix) section.
+
