+
+## Technical Appendix
+
+### Binary File Format
+
+Fastboot entries are stored in a binary format with the following structure:
+
+**Header (64 bytes)**:
+- Magic: `0x54425346` ("FSBT")
+- Version: `0x0001`
+- Entry count: Number of cores configured
+- CRC32 checksum for integrity
+
+**Entry (24 bytes per core)**:
+- Core ID (0-15)
+- Entry address (64-bit)
+- Flags (reserved)
+
+### Embedding Location
+
+When `FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT=yes`:
+- Entries are embedded at offset `0x10` (16 bytes) in u-boot.bin
+- U-Boot must have a pre-allocated reservation area
+- Maximum size depends on `CONFIG_EMBEDDED_FASTBOOT_BLOB_SIZE`
+
+### Boot Flow
+
+1. TF-A (BL31) starts
+2. TF-A checks for fastboot entries at U-Boot offset 0x10
+3. If found and valid:
+   - TF-A loads each core's image
+   - TF-A sets entry points
+   - TF-A releases secondary cores
+4. TF-A boots Core 0 (U-Boot or custom image)
+5. All cores run simultaneously
+
+### File Locations
+
+After build:
+```
+iMX93/
+├── flash.bin                    # Final boot image
+├── u-boot-fastboot.bin          # U-Boot with embedded entries
+└── fastboot_entries.bin         # Standalone entries (if not embedded)
+```
diff --git a/iMX93/fastboot_2_rtos.mak b/iMX93/fastboot_2_rtos.mak
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..98911e6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/iMX93/fastboot_2_rtos.mak
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Fastboot configuration for 2 RTOS cores without U-Boot
+# If U-Boot is not used, set FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED to no,
+# and a dummy u-boot.bin will be generated to carry the fastboot entry.
+
+# Core 0 configuration, customerize these variables as needed
+CA_CORE0_IMG ?= ca55_rtos1_img.bin
+CA_CORE0_IMG_LOAD_ADDR ?= 0xD1000000
+
+# Core 1 configuration, customerize these variables as needed
+CA_CORE1_IMG ?= ca55_rtos0_img.bin
+CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR ?= 0xD0000000
+
+# Fastboot entry is not embeded into U-Boot image
+FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT ?= no
+
+# Note: When FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT=no, a dummy file with name
+# u-boot-fastboot.bin will be generated to carry the fastboot
+# entry data and the fastboot entry data will be written to this file
+# at the offset specified by FASTBOOT_ENTRY_DUMMY_OFFSET
diff --git a/iMX93/fastboot_uboot_1_rtos.mak b/iMX93/fastboot_uboot_1_rtos.mak
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..249987b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/iMX93/fastboot_uboot_1_rtos.mak
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Fastboot configuration for U-Boot + 1 RTOS core
+# If U-Boot is used, default Core0 image is U-Boot Image, so don't define core0 image
+# Embedded fastboot entry in U-Boot Image.
+
+# Core 0 is U-Boot by default, no need to configure it
+
+# Core 1 configuration, customerize these variables as needed
+CA_CORE1_IMG ?= ca55_rtos0_img.bin
+CA_CORE1_IMG_LOAD_ADDR ?= 0xD0000000
+
+# Fastboot entry is embeded into U-Boot image
+# When FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT=yes, the fastboot entry data
+# will be overlaid into u-boot.bin at the offset specified by
+# FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_OFFSET
+FASTBOOT_ENTRY_EMBEDDED_UBOOT ?= yes
diff --git a/iMX93/soc.mak b/iMX93/soc.mak
